# --- external material, provenance unconfirmed ---
# Third-party strategy research from a separate engagement. No authorship,
# copyright or license statement of its own; references source documents
# that are not in this repo. Nothing from it may enter git history until
# ownership/relicensing is confirmed and recorded in NOTICE.
# See docs/arch/license-audit-2026-08-27.md G8.
EXTERNAL STRATEGIES TO ONBOARD/

# --- research findings, strategy docs, P&L/backtest reports (operator law
# 2026-09-02: researched data, strategies and docs about them NEVER enter
# git — no exceptions, no `git add -f`; `make license-check` refuses any
# tracked file under this tree). Engine-generated research output lives
# here; third-party material stays in the external vault above.
docs/research/

# --- research one-shots (repo-side, never packaged) ---
# Hand-run authoring/mining scripts that record ONE research moment: not
# worker modules, not verbs, never imported by the package, no tests. They
# live here for the venv and the `import claude_worker.*` seam only. Their
# findings belong in docs/research/ (git-excluded, below — operator law
# 2026-09-02); their outputs are the sha256-named artifacts in
# ~/multivenue/artifacts/rulesets, which are the reproducible record.
# `tools_` is a RESERVED PREFIX inside claude-worker/: promotion out of this
# class is a MOVE INTO src/claude_worker/ — never an un-ignore. This is
# hygiene, NOT a provenance rule: these files are the operator's own
# Apache-2.0 work. See docs/arch/research-tools-exclusion-plan.md.
claude-worker/tools_*.py
claude-worker/tools_*.sh
# NOTE: THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md is deliberately NOT ignored. It is generated
# by `make license-deps` but must be committed: it has to ship beside every
# distributed binary, and an ignored file is one that can be missing at
# release time. Regenerate it, never hand-edit it.
